      "id": "agriculture",
      "name": "Agriculture",
      "short": "Agriculture",
      "icon": "🌾",
      "marks": 500,
      "why": "The science optional with the widest overlap into General Studies: the agriculture, food security, irrigation and subsidy sections of GS-III are most of Paper I's ground, and cropping patterns and land reform reach into GS-I. Rewards candidates who already have the background, since both papers are technical rather than discursive. Paper I is ecology, soils, agronomy, water management and horticulture; Paper II is genetics and plant breeding, plant physiology, biotechnology, plant protection and animal science.",
